    "title": "Material Bench (uniform)",
    "description": "Weapon/VFX bench: 9 materials (concrete, metal, stone, wood, brick, cardboard, fabric, plywood, glass), each an identical cell \u2014 3-wide/2-storey wall at gu y=2, matching 3x3 floor zone at y=4..6, one guard patrolling a 2-cell route at y=5 across the block's own x-span, one overhead light centred over the block at y=3. Spacing is a uniform 5 GU per material (x=2,7,12,17,22,27,32,37,42), unlike PLAYGROUND where the first four materials sit at Director-calibrated DIFFERENT distances (2026-08-19 ruling, concrete/metal/stone/wood at 2/4/6/9 GU) for impact-angle testing \u2014 that design intent is deliberate and this map does not replace or touch it (docs/... PLAYGROUND stays canon for calibration). PLAYGROUND_2 exists so every material can be captured/compared with the exact same geometry, guard offset and light, for the R3D-6 shot-VFX-flow bench (sparks, decals, soot) \u2014 INFILTRAITOR_AGENT_START_GU slides the capture along x (agent y stays 9 for every material) and the camera frames each one identically."
